src/nist_ai_100_1/schema/*.yaml, src/nist_ai_100_1/datamodel/ and project/
model the Artificial Intelligence Risk Management Framework (AI RMF 1.0),
which the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) publishes as
NIST AI 100-1, https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.AI.100-1 (January 2023). They
are this project's rendering, written in its own words with NIST as the source
of the definitions; they are not NIST's, and their use does not imply
endorsement by NIST.

NIST's statement on its works, read on 2026-11-05 at
https://www.nist.gov/open/copyright-fair-use-and-licensing-statements-srd-data-software-and-technical-series-publications,
says that works authored by NIST employees are not subject to copyright
protection within the United States. To the extent NIST may assert rights
outside the United States, it grants the public a non-exclusive, perpetual,
paid-up, royalty-free, worldwide right to reprint them in all formats,
including derivative works. It asks for its recommended citation followed by
"Republished courtesy of the National Institute of Standards and Technology."
The text the publication quotes from others, such as ISO, keeps its owners'
rights; this repository's own text does not repeat it.

upstream/NIST.AI.100-1.pdf is the publication, unchanged, and
src/nist_ai_100_1/data/ reprints its Tables 1 to 4 and takes short lists from
its Figure 3 and Appendix A:

  National Institute of Standards and Technology (2023), Artificial
