NIST's catalog and Playbook
---------------------------

upstream/oscal-content/ holds NIST's catalog of the AI RMF in the Open Security
Controls Assessment Language (OSCAL), retrieved from
https://github.com/usnistgov/oscal-content/tree/f0de6d8d8c059d374f15e0ae07508d82e370fc1d/nist.gov/AI100-1/ver1/json
(the v1.6.0 release), beside NIST's LICENSE.md from the root of the same commit.
Both files are identical to their counterparts there, and
scripts/check_upstream_release.py checks that they stay so. NIST's work is in
the public domain within the United States, and NIST dedicates it to the
worldwide public domain under CC0 1.0.

upstream/playbook.json is the NIST AI RMF Playbook's file, unchanged, from
https://airc.nist.gov/docs/playbook.json, read on 2026-11-05. NIST's statement
above covers it. The Playbook's entries and the resources they name are by many
authors, and each resource keeps its own terms; the catalogue carries their
titles and addresses as NIST's catalog gives them. src/nist_ai_100_1/data/ holds
the catalog's Playbook material with the Playbook file's tags.

